#import "/modern-iaf/manuals/text/en/f35i/ch2/src.typ": *

The #jet.short takes fuel in the air from a tanker's boom, through a receptacle on its back (@fuel). The sim has no tanker: this whole section is #term("not modelled"). The cockpit procedure is in the F-35's flight manual, which is not public: open. Two public rules touch it:

- On the ground the crew and the pilot have a hand signal for opening and closing the receptacle's door#afi[paragraph 3.2.3]. Inferred: the door is tried on the ground before a flight that will refuel.
- After a refuelling the pilot does the checks of the cruise again: the cautions and the fuel first (@cruise-checks)#afi[paragraph 3.14.1].

Inferred from the F-16's procedure: the weapons are made safe before the jet closes on the tanker, the door is opened before contact and closed after it, and the fuel is checked when the jet has left the boom.
